# OpenPak console DNS: every Nintendo name a Wii U / 3DS / Wii / DS asks for resolves to the
# OpenPak box, so a console that only lets you set a DNS server (no CFW) still lands here.
# Also answers the *.openpak.org names the patched consoles (nn-inkay, nn-nimbus) use.
SSSL_UDP_PORT=53
SSSL_DNS_DEFAULT_ADDRESS=145.241.199.19
# The second NAT check server lives on the status box.
SSSL_DNS_MAP_nncs2.app.nintendowifi.net=145.241.228.207
SSSL_DNS_MAP_nncs2.app.openpak.org=145.241.228.207
# NP-4: the family list comes from the same map the emulators read — the
# website's network profile. The default is the website on this box; the
# compiled-in list covers the website being down.
NETPROFILE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:20010/api/v1/network/profile
# Signed redirect ceiling (docs/signed-ceiling.md): fetched from the pinned
# https://openpak.org/api/v1/network/ceiling and cached here with the highest
# version ever accepted. Mount a volume on it so rollback protection and the
# cached ceiling survive a container restart. Default: ~/.openpak-sssl-dns.
SSSL_DNS_STATE_DIR=/home/node/.openpak-sssl-dns
# Abuse limits (dns/README.md): the defaults suit consoles; uncomment to change.
# SSSL_DNS_RATE=20
# SSSL_DNS_BURST=200
# SSSL_DNS_SLIP=2
# SSSL_DNS_IPV4_PREFIX=24
# SSSL_DNS_IPV6_PREFIX=56
# SSSL_DNS_MAX_UDP=1232
# SSSL_DNS_NEGATIVE_TTL=30
# SSSL_DNS_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=2000
# SSSL_DNS_STATS_INTERVAL=3600
